.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
# `node_modules` alone matches only the repository root. `web/node_modules`
# was therefore COPYied into the frontend stage, shadowing what `npm ci` had
# just installed from the lockfile -- the container built against whatever
# the host happened to have. Harmless while the two agreed; a hard build
# failure the moment they did not:
#
#   Cannot start service: Host version "0.27.3" does not match binary
#   version "0.28.2"
#
# `**/node_modules` matches at any depth, which is what was meant.
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/.svelte-kit
tests/
kb/
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.claude
*.egg
dist/
build/
